[{"text":"ThreeDivergence[exp, CV[p, i]] calculates the partial derivative of exp w.r.t. p^i.","anchor":"threedivergence"},{"text":"ThreeDivergence[exp, CV[p, i], CV[p,i], ...] gives the multiple derivative.","anchor":"threedivergence"},{"text":"Owing to the fact that in FeynCalc dummy Cartesian index are always understood to be upper indices, applying ThreeDivergence to an expression is equivalent to the action of \\nabla^i = \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial p^i}.","anchor":"threedivergence"},{"text":"Overview, FourDivergence.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"CSP[p, q] ThreeDivergence[%, CV[q, i]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^i\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSP[p - k, q] ThreeDivergence[%, CV[k, i]]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(\\overline{p}-\\overline{k})\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\overline{q}^i\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CFAD[{p, m^2}, p - q] ThreeDivergence[%, CVD[p, i]]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p^2+m^2-i \\eta ).((p-q)^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{2 q^i-2 p^i}{(p^2+m^2-i \\eta ).((p-q)^2-i \\eta )^2}-\\frac{2 p^i}{(p^2+m^2-i \\eta )^2.((p-q)^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Differentiation of \\(3\\)-vectors living in different dimensions (\\(3\\), D-1, \\(D-4\\)) works only in the t’Hooft-Veltman scheme","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ThreeDivergence[CVD[p, i], CV[p, j]]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{\\$Aborted}\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ThreeDivergence[CVD[p, i], CV[p, j]]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\delta }^{ij}\\]","anchor":"cb6-1","section":"Examples"}]